# Files NOT uploaded to Google Cloud Build by `gcloud builds submit` (mirrors .dockerignore).
# Top-level folders are anchored with a leading slash: a bare `data` would also match app/web/static/data/ (needed by the app).
# Without this file gcloud would fall back to .gitignore and upload docs, tests and PDFs needlessly.
.gcloudignore
.git
.gitignore
.github
.venv
venv
**/__pycache__
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
/data
/results
/dist
# hackathon report, PDF and figures (contain dataset images): never uploaded to Cloud Build
/submission
/tests
/docs
/deploy
*.pdf
phases.md
eval_P1_*.md
# checkpoints never enter the image; Cloud Run mounts the runtime one from a private bucket at /models
weights/*
!weights/README.md
app/*.pyi
.env
.env.*
